  "interpretation": {
    "give_back_is_real_but_concentrated": "The 31.7% 'capture rate' headline is misleading and must not be quoted as an inefficiency: it sums every trade's best unrealised moment, and no strategy can exit every trade at its exact peak. The honest figure is that only 29 of 664 trades (4%) hand back more than 0.5R from their peak - but those give back ~2.98R each, roughly 87R against a 244R book. So the user's concern is real and material, just concentrated in a small minority of trades.",
    "why_profit_exits_still_fail": "Take-profit and give-back stops cut the reversion move that pays for the losers. This book wins by holding until the bounce completes (IBS>0.8 already detects that); capping the winner at a fixed R removes the right tail while leaving every loser intact. Same structural reason breakeven+partials destroyed the champion engine, and it is why WIN RATE rises on these variants while net R falls - a textbook sign of a bad exit that feels good.",
    "pre_registered_verdict": "REJECTED. The pre-registered rule was: pick the best variant on discovery, validate on holdout. P4_tp1.5_and_6d won discovery (89.0R vs 75.2R) and produced 153.4R on holdout versus a 153.43R baseline - no improvement. Rejected, and the pick is not re-chosen after seeing the holdout.",
    "honest_lead_not_a_result": "P1_take_profit_1.5u beats baseline on BOTH halves independently (disc 80.7 vs 75.2, hold 157.8 vs 153.4). That is suggestive, but it was NOT the pre-registered selection and 13 variants were tested, so it is a lead for a future out-of-sample test - not a promotable result.",
    "important_interaction": "Adding a take-profit to the 6-day time stop ERASES the time stop's gain: 6d alone holds out at 164.1R, 6d+tp1.5 at 153.4R. The two do not compose - the validated change remains the time stop ALONE."
